WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.149
Weak encryption undermines the confidentiality customers expect from a SaaS provider.

2
00:00:05.149 --> 00:00:14.228
Teams should avoid outdated algorithms, custom cryptography, hard-coded secrets, poor randomness, and weak password hashing practices.

3
00:00:14.228 --> 00:00:22.400
Missing or misconfigured TLS can expose credentials, session tokens, API traffic, and customer data in transit.

4
00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:30.881
Secure certificate handling and modern transport settings must be consistent across web apps, APIs, services, and integrations.

5
00:00:30.881 --> 00:00:34.154
Poor key management can defeat otherwise strong encryption.

6
00:00:34.154 --> 00:00:42.146
Keys need protected storage, limited access, rotation, lifecycle management, and separation from the data they protect.

7
00:00:42.146 --> 00:00:52.154
Sensitive data exposure can also happen through logs, exports, backups, debug output, cached responses, and excessive API responses.

8
00:00:52.154 --> 00:00:56.514
Applications should minimize sensitive data and control where it appears.

9
00:00:56.514 --> 00:00:59.667
Use strong encryption standards and vetted libraries.

10
00:00:59.667 --> 00:01:03.319
Handle certificates and TLS configuration securely.

11
00:01:03.319 --> 00:01:06.722
Manage keys through protected, access-controlled processes.

12
00:01:06.722 --> 00:01:10.793
Selected SOC 2 mappings for this topic include CC6.

13
00:01:10.793 --> 00:01:13.487
7 - Data protection; CC6.

14
00:01:13.487 --> 00:01:15.263
8 - Transmission protection.
